# ── Mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With nothing set, the site runs in DEMO mode: an in-memory store seeded
# with one campaign, free claims that run the real reserve and mark-paid
# path, no secrets. Setting SUPABASE_URL switches the whole site to LIVE
# mode; each payment rail then switches on with its own group below.
# Copy to .env.local first.

# ── Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown in the header and on Stripe line items.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=starter-fundraise
# Where this site lives. Stripe redirects back here after checkout.
# http://localhost:3000 locally, your domain in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Ledger (Supabase, server-only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Run docs/schema.sql once. RLS is on with no policies, so only the service
# role key can read or write. Setting SUPABASE_URL is what turns live mode on.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Back-of-house password for the two /api/admin routes (sent as x-admin-key).
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ── Card payments (Stripe Connect, server-only) ──────────────────────────
# Stripe > Developers > API keys. sk_test_ while rehearsing, sk_live_ when real.
# The platform account charges the buyer, keeps the course fee as the
# application fee and transfers the rest to the athlete's connected account.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Local:  `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook`
#         and copy the whsec_ it prints.
# Live:   Stripe > Developers > Webhooks > your endpoint > Signing secret.
# These are two different secrets. The live one will not verify local events.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── USDC payments (Privy + an RPC, server-only unless marked) ────────────
# Privy dashboard > your app > Settings > Basics. Enable Email as a login
# method, enable Ethereum embedded wallets, add your domain to Allowed origins.
# The app id is read on the server and passed to the client as a prop.
PRIVY_APP_ID=
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=
# "base-sepolia" to rehearse with testnet USDC, "base" for real money. The
# browser and the server read this same value, so the buyer signs on the
# chain the server verifies against.
NEXT_PUBLIC_USDC_CHAIN=base-sepolia
# An HTTPS RPC for that chain. The server reads transaction receipts here.
USDC_RPC_URL=

# The course fee recipient is not an env var on purpose. It lives in
# lib/course-fee.ts and is a default. Live mode refuses to
# start if it is the zero address.
